The commit-time GC (pipapo_gc) freed expired elements before the live pointer (priv->match) was swapped to the clone copy. This could cause use-after-free because concurrent readers (packet path, dump) might still access the old version of the data structure containing those elements. The fix splits GC into a scan phase (only unlinks and collects elements) and a reclaim phase (called after the pointer swap), ensuring no readers can see freed memory.

